# GL features that an MC2_* gate drives and whose VK twin lacks (tools/gl_vk_feature_coverage.py).
# Format: gate | GL shader | WHY   (one line per pair; '#' starts a comment)
#
# Discipline, mirroring tools/glsl_port_diff.allowlist:
#   * a NOT_PORTED row with no entry here is a NEW gap and fails the check;
#   * an entry whose row is no longer NOT_PORTED is STALE and fails the check (delete it);
#   * `py -3 tools/gl_vk_feature_coverage.py --flip-check BASE` fails a commit that turns the
#     default of a gate listed here ON, because the flip would change GL only.
# Only HIGH-confidence rows are enforced; MEDIUM rows are advisory (docs/gl-vk-feature-coverage.md).
# Lines whose WHY says "no such name in the VK twin" state only what the tool established: the name
# is absent from the VK shaders, island C++ and gpu_abi. Nobody has yet checked whether VK computes
# the same thing under another name; do that before porting or before deleting an entry.

# --- Gates ALREADY default ON in GL: the drift is live today
